+
+.. namedconf:statement:: update-fix-names
+   :tags: zone
+   :short: Normalizes hostname bytes in dynamic updates to a primary zone (local extension).
+
+   This local extension is disabled by default and is available only in
+   primary zone statements. When enabled, owner names below the zone apex
+   and PTR targets are normalized during dynamic update processing,
+   including prerequisites and deletions. Authorization uses the normalized
+   names. The original authenticated message is not modified.
+
+   ASCII letters, digits, and interior hyphens are retained. Other bytes
+   become hyphens inside labels or ``x`` at label boundaries. Label lengths
+   and case are preserved. The owner name's zone suffix and leading wildcard
+   label are retained. RDATA other than PTR targets is unchanged.
+
+   Enable this only in dedicated DHCP hostname zones: service labels such as
+   ``_sip._tcp`` would also be changed. Different input names can map to the
+   same output name; this option does not resolve collisions. Existing zone
+   data and queries are not normalized. Retain the usual update authorization
+   settings and enable this option in both forward and reverse zones.
 
